;; docker/pgbouncer/userlist.txt.example — TEMPLATE (P2.1b T11)
;;
;; The real file is docker/pgbouncer/userlist.txt (gitignored — it carries a
;; credential). Only the auth_user needs an entry: every other role
;; (gremion, future per-tenant roles) is verified via auth_query against the
;; SCRAM verifier stored in Postgres (docker/pgbouncer/pgbouncer-auth.sql).
;;
;; Render at deploy (S4) from .env's PGBOUNCER_AUTH_PASSWORD — see
;; docs/runbooks/pgbouncer.md. Plaintext is accepted here: PgBouncer uses it
;; to log in to Postgres as pgbouncer_auth (and for its admin console).
;; chmod 600 the rendered file.
"pgbouncer_auth" "CHANGE_ME_pgbouncer_auth"
